Note: kyverno-test's chart kyverno has 11 Helm hooks for upgrade, delete or test, among them Jobs kyverno-migrate-resources, kyverno-rm-webhooks, kyverno-scale-to-zero. They are left out, as cub helm leaves them out, because only Helm runs them.

Live on your management cluster: kyverno-prod, kyverno-test, kyverno-uat. Each delivery profile deploys the same objects to the same cluster. apply also writes handover.sh, which steps each live profile aside without removing anything, so the delivery profiles carry on alone; run it after apply.sh. See "If your profiles are live" in docs/user/onboard-your-sveltos-fleet.md.

Next: cub sveltos apply <the same input and options> --out <dir>, read <dir>/apply.sh, then run it.

== 0/6 Check before changing anything

== 1/6 One named Target per cluster, in mer-targets

== 2/6 One component per profile: a base holding what its charts and policies render to, and a rollout workflow

== 3/6 One variant per cluster, each holding what its base holds

== 4/6 The management cluster's record: one delivery profile per variant

== 5/6 Release each variant, stage by stage: promote, approve, publish

== 6/6 Point Sveltos at ConfigHub (your management cluster)
